# Wireframe: Issue Detail — Status Dropdown

> **Version:** 1.0.1
> **Changelog:** Added standalone Toast component cross-reference. Clarified i18n scope as single-locale. (PATCH)

## Purpose & Flow Context

Allows the user to transition an issue through the workflow by selecting a new status from a dropdown. Serves the "Change Issue Status" flow step. Entry: user on `/issues/:id` clicks status badge. Exit: user remains on same page with updated status.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown trigger |
| `[●]` | Status color dot | `[↻]` | Loading spinner |
| `[!]` | Error / alert | `[✓]` | Success |
| `────────` | Divider / separator |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `main` for content region |
| Heading order | h1 issue title, h2 section headings |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm.

**App-shell**: Shared header + sidebar + main container. The issue detail page sits in the main content region.

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Status badge + dropdown (primary action for this change)
2. Back button + issue identifier
3. Issue title (h1)
4. Priority + metadata
5. Description + labels
6. Action buttons (Edit, Delete)
7. Comments section

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [← Back]   [>Todo▼]          [●] No priority                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                     |
|  ENG-1                                                              |
|                                                                     |
|  Implement login page                                               |
|  ====================                                               |
|                                                                     |
|  [● In Progress]  [>▼]      Urgent                                 |
|                                                                     |
|  Assignee: Juan     Created: Jul 21    Updated: Jul 21              |
|                                                                     |
|  frontend  feature                                                   |
|                                                                     |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────          |
|  Description                                                        |
|                                                                     |
|  Add login page with email/password and OAuth providers...          |
|                                                                     |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────          |
|                                                                     |
|  [Edit]  [Delete]                                                   |
|                                                                     |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────          |
|  Comments (3)                                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [Button] [>Dropdown] [●] StatusDot*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Status badge trigger | IssueStatusBadge | Click opens dropdown list; shows current status with color dot. On selection: sends PATCH /issues/{id}/status, shows spinner on badge. On success: badge updates to new status color. On error: badge reverts, error toast | Loading: spinner replaces arrow, dropdown disabled. Error 422: revert + error toast. Network error: revert + error toast |
| Status dropdown list | Select (reused) | Positioned below badge. Lists all workflow statuses. Arrow keys navigate, Enter selects, Escape closes | Click outside closes. Empty state not applicable (workflow statuses always available) |
| Toast | Toast | Slides in from right on transition result. Success: green left border, "Status updated to {name}". Error: red left border, error message from API | Auto-dismisses after 5s. Manual dismiss with X |

### ToastNotification (standalone component)

| Property | Details |
|----------|---------|
| DS component | Toast |
| Purpose | Feedback for status transition results (success/error) |
| Placement | Top-right overlay, slides in |
| Variants | `success` — green left border, check icon; `error` — red left border, X icon |
| States | Visible (auto-dismiss after 5s), dismissing (slide-out), hidden |
| Edge cases | Multiple rapid transitions queue toasts; manual dismiss via X button |
| a11y | `role="alert"` for error toasts, live region for announcements |

## Data Display

No table/list. The status is a single-value selector displayed as a colored pill.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Status badge (default) | Current workflow stage | Color-coded: grey=backlog/todo, blue=in-progress, green=done, grey=canceled |
| Status dropdown options | Available workflow stages | All statuses visible: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, Done, Canceled |
| Toast success | Confirmation of change | "Status updated to In Progress" |
| Toast error | Explain invalid transition | Display API error message like "Invalid transition: Cannot move from Todo to Done directly" |

**i18n scope:** Single-locale (English). Text expansion room and RTL layout not considered.

## States

### Populated (Default)

Issue is loaded with a status. The badge shows the current status name with its color dot. Clicking opens the dropdown.

```
+-------------------------+
|  [● In Progress]  [>▼]  |
+-------------------------+
```

### Loading

When a status transition is in flight, the dropdown arrow is replaced by a small spinner. The dropdown is closed and the trigger is disabled.

```
+-------------------------+
|  [● In Progress]  [↻]   |
+-------------------------+
```

### Success

After a successful transition, the badge updates to the new status color and name. A success toast slides in at the top-right.

```
+-------------------------+
|  [● Done]  [>▼]          |
+-------------------------+

+-- Toast (top-right) ---+
| ✓ Status updated to    |
|   Done                 |
+------------------------+
```

### Error

After a failed transition (422 BUSINESS_RULE_ERROR or network error), the badge reverts to the previous status. An error toast shows the message.

```
+-------------------------+
|  [● In Progress]  [>▼]  |
+-------------------------+

+-- Toast (top-right) ---+
| ✗ Invalid transition    |
|   Cannot move from Todo |
|   to Done directly      |
+------------------------+
```

### Empty

Not applicable — a status is always present on an issue. If an issue somehow lacks a status, the badge shows "Unknown" in neutral color.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full layout, inline status badge |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same, dropdown remains inline |
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-width dropdown, touch targets ≥44px |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `main` contains issue detail content |
| Heading order | h1 for issue title, h2 for "Description" and "Comments" section headings |
| Reading / Focus order | Back → Status badge → Priority → Assignee → Metadata → Labels → Description → Edit/Delete → Comments |
| Accessible names | Status badge gets `aria-label="Status: {name}. Click to change"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab to badge, Enter/Space opens dropdown, Arrow keys to navigate, Enter selects, Escape closes. Tab moves to next element after dropdown closes |
| Target size | Status badge ≥32px height, ≥44px on mobile |
| Focus not obscured | Dropdown renders above content, no sticky regions overlap |
| Non-color intent | Status names are visible text in addition to colors. Error/success toasts include text, not just icon |
